From 1a4837f56a9554dee8f439ab5c2950f70261cedf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:23:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep containment release decisions with open
 authorities

Refuse terminal authorities when creating new containment episodes, and require authorities to release or explicitly retain their episodes before completing. Surface those episodes in worker context, including replica-only targets. Preserve unsafe descendant containment and producer release semantics.

Proof: regression suite red on main (8 failed), 628 focused tests passed with one schema-size failure then schema regression rerun green; ten behavioral mutants killed. Read-only hub replay: 11 held episodes across example boards, 10 terminal authority nominations refused if nominated now; lookup matches all 11. Ship verdict reader accepts containment_retained.
